codex
Rejected at Step 0: the paper supports generatable and exactly verifiable witnesses, but not a hard family under either track.

The strongest \(Y_r\) candidate collapses to a linear-time triangle-incidence test. It recovered the planted Kempe-frozen colouring on 20/20 randomly relabelled \(Y_{40}\) instances, with at most 1,570 primitive operations. The compact route is essentially identical, so Track B also lacks a meaningful compression gap.

The proposed hidden-swap family is unsupported by a distributional hardness result. Worst-case PSPACE-completeness of Kempe Reachability does not establish hardness for inverse-planted random walks; meanwhile, the paper’s \(P_4\)-free regime has a constructive polynomial algorithm and \(2n\log n\) diameter bound. See the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.00695) and its cited [Kempe-reachability complexity result](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304397520303169).

The complete, measured decision is in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.00695/REJECTED.md). Per the task instructions, no generator or synthetic gate artifacts were created after the Step-0 rejection.
